      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/julidochromis-transcriptus",
      "html": "<p>The masked julie, Julidochromis transcriptus, is a small cichlid endemic to the rocky coastal zones of northwestern Lake Tanganyika. It is known from between Luhanga and Makabola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo and grows to around 65 mm SL.</p><ul><li>Space: medium tank</li><li>Social: best in a pair</li><li>Compatibility: choose tankmates carefully</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/julidochromis-transcriptus",
      "html": "<p>Endemic to northwestern Lake Tanganyika, between Luhanga and Makabola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, with type locality given simply as the 'extreme north' of the lake.</p><p>In Lake Tanganyika this species is recorded at Luhanga.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/julidochromis-transcriptus",
      "html": "<p>Inhabits rocky, coastal zones.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/julidochromis-transcriptus",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: Julidochromis: from the name 'Julidini', a putative tribe of labrid marine wrasses which Julidochromis resemble, and the Greek chromis, meaning 'fish'. transcriptus: from the Latin transcribo, meaning 'transcribed, copied'.</p>"
    }
